\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RidentRefvarInsert
< m1: NPPROP{NPPROPrec1}
            [  mu1,
               idrel/T2,
               I2: mu2,
               I3: mu3
            ]

  m2: T1 
>

< m : NPPROP{NPPROPrec1}
            [ mu1,
              idrel/T2,
              I2: mu2,
              I4: tempadvrel/T1,
              I3: mu3
            ]
>
   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I2: ALL (mu2, locadvrel/..)
       I3: QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu3) AND
           QUOTE_tempretronotfound(mu3) AND
           QUOTE_tempdurnotfound(mu3) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu3, [I31:rel1/..])
         I31: rel1 IN [tempadvrel, locadvrel]
       I4: T1.CAT IN [ADVPVAR, PREPPVAR, SENTENCEVAR]
       m2: T1.CAT IN [ADVPVAR, PREPPVAR, SENTENCEVAR]
      >

<
   SUBRULE (* 1. ADVPVAR *)
      < T1: ADVPVAR{ADVPVARrec1} >
      < T1: ADVPVAR{ADVPVARrec1} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: ADVPVARrec1.class = reference AND
              ADVPVARrec1.retro = false
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: ADVPVARrec1.class = reference AND
              ADVPVARrec1.retro = false
          A1: @
         >

   SUBRULE (* 2. PREPPVAR *)
      < T1: PREPPVAR{PREPPVARrec1} >
      < T1: PREPPVAR{PREPPVARrec1} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: PREPPVARrec1.class = reference AND
              PREPPVARrec1.retro = false
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: PREPPVARrec1.class = reference AND
              PREPPVARrec1.retro = false
          A1: @
         >

   SUBRULE (* 3. SENTENCEVAR *)
      < T1: SENTENCEVAR{SENTENCEVARrec1} >
      < T1: SENTENCEVAR{SENTENCEVARrec1} >

      COMP
         <

          C1: SENTENCEVARrec1.conjclass = reference AND
              SENTENCEVARrec1.conjretro = false
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: SENTENCEVARrec1.conjclass = reference AND
              SENTENCEVARrec1.conjretro = false
          A1: @
         >
>

&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RidentRefvarInsert
\item[* relevant examples:]
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] IdentPropFormation
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) RC\_
IdentTempVarInsert
\item[* date of creation:] 7-SEP-1988 16:47:36  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch RIdentRefvarInsertion
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 23/10/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Adapted rule so that it will work in a large iterative class containing all 
advvarr insertion rules. Especially:\\
1) there is only one var-extraction order in analysis (i.e.\ tempadv - locadv - 
sentadv), correlated with the actual surface order of the vars (which is 
sentadv (momentarily only in leftdislocrel) - locadv - tempadv), so there is 
right to left extraction)\\
2) in generation, there are more orders possible for insertion (depending on 
source language)\\
3) the surface order for elements of the same class remains the same over 
languages, with obligatory left to right insertion (locadv1 - locadv2 - locadv3 
etc) = right to left extraction
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] isomorphism with other subgrammars
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) Note that for 
identificationals, only one kind of tempadv is allowed (a refvar). In case more 
tempadvs are allowed, mu2 must be allowed to harbour these as well, with 
perhaps a restriction on the kind of tempadv(s) allowed there.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
