\item[* date of creation:] 7-MAR-1989 
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch Ridentsadvvar
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 23/10/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Adapted rule to make it work in one large iterative advvar rule class: sentadvs 
are the last advvars to be removed from the sentence in nalysis (in generation, 
the insertion order is determined by the source language). See the remarks made 
under RIdentRefVarInsert.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:]
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) There may be 
only one leftdislocrel, so a combination of a sentadv and a conjsent there is 
impossible
($^{*}$Because he refused, probably this is the best solution). Another
position for sentadvs must be formulated using the attribute `position' 
of advs (However, this is not used yet). 
